_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 16
---
order: 16
---
short_label: XI.16
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two parallel planes are cut by any plane, then their intersections are parallel.
----
proof:

Let the two parallel planes *AB* and *CD* be cut by the plane *EFGH,* and let *EF* and *GH* be their intersections. [!just XI.3]

I say that *EF* is parallel to *GH.*

If not, then *EF* and *GH* will, when produced, meet either in the direction of *F* and *H* or in the direction of *E* and *G.*

<figure class="diagram">
